# `Mailer` falls under ARCHITECTURE.md's own documented exception to
# trait-impl-colocation ("unless the trait is part of the public API
# contract ... or test mocking"): it exists precisely so `StubMailer` can
# stand in for `SmtpMailer` in tests without a live relay (src/mailer.rs:19-32
# WHY block), and `StubMailer` is `pub` for that reason (src/mailer.rs:106-110).
# `epistole` is also a single `[package]` (Cargo.toml has no `[workspace]`
# table), so the rule's prescribed fix -- move the trait to the lowest crate
# that calls through it -- has no target crate to move to; splitting one into
# existence solely to relocate this trait would be a contrived structural
# change with no isolation benefit, the same anti-pattern the standard warns
# against in the opposite direction. See epistole#108.
ARCHITECTURE/trait-impl-colocation:src/mailer.rs
